secutive quarters at any point before end-2032 WHILE GDP-weighted OECD-38 core inflation stays above 2.5% over the same four quarters (the conjunction matters: unemployment alone would be an ordinary cycle).\",\"by_when\":\"End-2032.\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The AI mismatch channel is materially larger than the +0.56 pp I computed, and the shrinking-labour-force pull of -0.7 pp is not offsetting it — i.e. displaced cognitive workers are neither re-absorbed nor retiring. Cut CQ1 to 4-6 (conjunct A's 0.52 collapses toward 0.15). Raise CQ6-C by 5 points, since simultaneous high unemployment and high core inflation IS the stagflationary-squeeze signature, taking those points from B. Cut CQ3 P50 to ~1.2%/yr. Raise hypothesis plank (c) only if the inflation leg then rolls over, which this signpost does not by itself establish.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 1 fermi seat, effort 'labor'."}}